.TH git-global 1  "git-global 0.8.0" 
.SH NAME
git\-global \- Keep track of all the git repositories on your machine.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit\-global\fR [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-j\fR|\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-u\fR|\fB\-\-untracked\fR] [\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-nountracked\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Keep track of all the git repositories on your machine.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Read configuration from FILE instead of the default gitconfig.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose mode.
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-json\fR
Output subcommand results in JSON.
.TP
\fB\-u\fR, \fB\-\-untracked\fR
Show untracked files in output.
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-nountracked\fR
Don\*(Aqt show untracked files in output.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
git\-global\-ahead(1)
Shows repos with changes that are not pushed to a remote
.TP
git\-global\-ignore(1)
Ignores a repo, removing it from the list
.TP
git\-global\-ignored(1)
Lists all ignored repos
.TP
git\-global\-info(1)
Shows meta\-information about git\-global
.TP
git\-global\-install\-manpage(1)
Attempts to install git\-global\*(Aqs man page
.TP
git\-global\-list(1)
Lists all known repos
.TP
git\-global\-scan(1)
Updates cache of known repos
.TP
git\-global\-staged(1)
Shows git index status for repos with staged changes
.TP
git\-global\-stashed(1)
Shows repos with stashed changes
.TP
git\-global\-status(1)
Shows status (`git status \-s`) for repos with any changes
.TP
git\-global\-unstaged(1)
Shows working dir status for repos with unstaged changes
.TP
git\-global\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
